 than the final goal: `350 * 1/2` which brings `red` hue down to 150, green and blue up a little:\n   \n   [ begin{aligned}\n   150 + left(frac{1/2} {255}right)(1-|1-frac{350} {255}|) = frac{303150} {5100} = 12.031714330895868\n   end{aligned} ]\n\n8. **Resolving the Issue:**\n   - Then, adding a correction adjustment of `1` makes the red hue parameter to be exactly 12. There might be a consensus that adding 1 is the maximum conflict allowable in order not to make the tint parameter change.\n\nTherefore, the largest reduction that can be made to the red hue parameter without decreasing the shade or tint from their original values is:\n\n[ boxed{12} ]",
